---
import SectionHeading from "@/components/SectionHeading.astro"
import SectionLabel from "@/components/SectionLabel.astro"
import { RAINBOW } from "@/lib/rainbow"
---

<section
  id="about"
  class="mx-auto max-w-4xl scroll-mt-20 px-6 py-16"
  style={{ "--accent": RAINBOW[3] }}
>
  <SectionHeading accent={RAINBOW[3]}>About</SectionHeading>
  <div class="space-y-4 text-foreground">
    <p>
      Hi, I don't know if you're reading this in a personal or professional
      context, so I'll try to make this summary (and website) applicable to
      both. In short, I'm a software engineer who branches out into other fields
      of engineering, mostly electrical engineering for now. I have been working
      professionally since 2022, in large corporations and small startups, doing
      consistent bug triage and feature additions, as well as large, impactful
      refactors and build-outs of new products, utilizing new models, services,
      and third-party integrations.
    </p>
    <p class="space-y-4 text-foreground">
      I first got into programming when my dad handed me a book and bought me a
      gaming PC when I was 9 years old. I only worked my way up to if-statements
      before I kinda put it down, but that was enough for me. Eventually I
      started modding games to have fun with them, and when I needed to upgrade
      my PC, I would learn about computers and how they worked while I did the
      install. After high school, I decided to take this route seriously, but
      instead of going into IT, I decided to pursue a degree in computer
      science.
    </p>
    <p class="space-y-4 text-foreground">
      During my time in college, while interacting with engineering students
      from other disciplines, I gained in interest in what they do, the problems
      they have to solve, and the things that they make possible. This is likely
      what led me to be interested in engineering as a whole, and not just want
      to focus on one field. Through this interest, my passion for cars and
      engines sort of evolved as well, and I especially gained an interest in
      drag racing. The focus, consistency, and millisecond precision required in
      events like bracket racing, problems they have to solve and how they do
      them, how teams find the gray areas in classes to gain an advantage, all
      stood out to me.
    </p>
    <p class="space-y-4 text-foreground">
      Lately, I've been spending my off-hours on various projects. For example,
      I've been speccing out and installing a new audio system in my car, with
      testing microphones so I can tune the DSP to get a consistent EQ. I've
      also been installing modifications to my car (a Mustang GT) and developing
      ways to control them remotely, without having to take apart the interior
      to wire control signals.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
